{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794528206170,"sessionID":"ses_e2dcb0a25ffeKDrFVYdzDGhvxv","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2375985001Hyf7GLc1UQl1NY","sessionID":"ses_e2dcb0a25ffeKDrFVYdzDGhvxv","messageID":"msg_1d237444a001JheBImZQNHAYPy","type":"tool","id":"call_9a760a39275e4d31bc48d151","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n \"command-spec-kit-(plan|complete|implement|resume)\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/spec.md specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/plan.md | head -30","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/spec.md:61:A model that reads the hook brief sees `use command-speckit-save` or `use command-spec-kit-plan`, a raw scorer id that names no slash command and no policy. The public recommendation carries a `command` field only when a hub attaches one, and it never carries a policy, a kind or an owner, so a caller cannot tell whether to run, start or ask. When the daemon is down, the local Python scorer returns command rows such as `command-create-readme` for a plain prompt, and nothing says what a degraded brief may show.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/spec.md:78:{\"skillId\":\"command-spec-kit-plan\",\"score\":0.563727,\"confidence\":0.823,\"uncertainty\":0.16,\"dominantLane\":\"explicit_author\",\"status\":\"active\"}\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/spec.md:84:Advisor: live; use command-spec-kit-plan 0.82/0.16 pass.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/spec.md:111:[\"command-s