l-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill_advisor.py:2374:HAND_AUTHORED_COMMAND_BRIDGE_OWNER_NORMALIZATION = {\n$ rg -n 'readonly routingEnabled' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/projection.ts\n66:  readonly routingEnabled?: boolean;\n$ rg -c 'command-spec-kit-(plan|complete|implement|resume)\\b' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/holdout-prompts.jsonl .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/fixtures .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/holdout-prompts.jsonl:1\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/fixtures/skill-advisor-regression-cases.jsonl:1\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/fixtures/gate2-golden-prompts.jsonl:1\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/parity/fixtures/local-native-approved-divergences.json:2\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/scorer/same-owner-ambiguity.vitest.ts:2\n$ rg -n 'command-spec|memory:save|command-memory-save' AGENTS.md | wc -l\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"sed -n '100,125p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/spec.md\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794528251538,"end":1794528251826}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794528251849,"sessionID":"ses_e2dcb0a25ffeKDrFVYdzDGhvxv","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2380b02002lN01pf8zj9LtCk","sessionID":"ses_e2dcb0a25ffeKDrFVYdzDGhvxv","messageID":"msg_1d237a52e00166lB1R3Fs2AVbb","type":"tool","id":"call_38db21cffcce44978a7fbd45","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n \"Python|python\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/spec.md | head -30","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"61:A model that reads the hook brief sees `use command-speckit-save` or `use command-spec-kit-plan`, a raw scorer id that names no slash command and no policy. The public recommendation carries a `command` field only when a hub attaches one, and it never carries a policy, a kind or an owner, so a caller cannot tell whether to run, start or ask. When the daemon is down, the local Python scorer returns command rows such as `command-create-readme` for a plain prompt, and nothing says what a degraded brief may show.\n95:$ SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_FORCE_LOCAL=1 python3 .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill_advisor.py 'create a readme for the utils folder' | jq -c '[.[0:3][] | {skill, kind, source, passes_threshold}]'\n96:Native advisor unavailable (FORCE_LOCAL; freshness=unavailable); falling back to local Python scorer.\n109:{\"status\":\"fresh\",\"counts\":{\"commandMetadata\":23,\"allowList\":4,\"doctorRoutes\":35,\"generated\":62,\"typescriptActive\":45,\"pythonActive\":51}}\n112:$ jq -c '[.python[].id | select(test(\"spec-kit\"))]' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json\n186:- A stated contract for a degraded result. The local Python scorer returns `command-create-readme` as a passing row for a plain prompt.\n187:- The four allow-list ids, the Python `\"/prompt\"` lexical row and owner branch, the two Python hand-authored constants and the optional `routingEnabled` type.\n201:- Retire the allow-list file, its four ids and the Python `/prompt` residue, delete the Python hand-authored constants and make `routingEnabled` required (L7).\n213:- The Python-only ids `command-spec-kit-deep-research` and `command-spec-kit-deep-review`, the TypeScript compatibility ids `create:agent` and `create:manual-testing-playbook`, and the alias folds that map old ids onto live ones. The operator chose to rename only the four allow-list ids.\n214:- Typed `/memory:save` as prompt vocabulary in `explicit.ts`, `fusion.ts`, the Python scorer and the Gate 3 classifier. It matches what a user types, and five labelled corpus rows type it.\n231:| `ADV/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json` | Modify | Four Python rows and one owner key deleted |\n266:| REQ-010 | The Python `\"/prompt\"` lexical row and the `command == \"/prompt\"` owner branch are deleted. The alias folds in `aliases.ts` and the Python alias table stay. |\n267:| REQ-011 | `HAND_AUTHORED_COMMAND_BRIDGES` and `HAND_AUTHORED_COMMAND_BRIDGE_OWNER_NORMALIZATION` are deleted from the Python scorer. `CommandBridgeProjection.routingEnabled` is required and `scoringCommandBridges` keeps rows with `routingEnabled === true`. |\n346:| Scope | 14/25 | About 24 files and 700 lines across the deriver, the handler, the renderer, the CLI, the Python scorer and tests |\n361:- How far does the id retirement go? Decision: \"Rename the four, drop /prompt (Recommended)\". The four allow-list ids become `command-speckit-*`, the Python `/prompt` residue goes, the alias folds stay, and the Python deep ids and the TypeScript `create:*` compatibility ids stay as a recorded limitation. REQ-018 does not need their rename, because `COMMAND_ROWS` keys `create:agent` and `create:manual-testing-playbook` as they are, so both carry `ownerSkillId` `sk-doc`.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"61:A model that reads the hook brief sees `use command-speckit-save` or `use command-spec-kit-plan`, a raw scorer id that names no slash command and no policy. The public recommendation carries a `command` field only when a hub attaches one, and it never carries a policy, a kind or an owner, so a caller cannot tell whether to run, start or ask. When the daemon is down, the local Python scorer returns command rows such as `command-create-readme` for a plain prompt, and nothing says what a degraded brief may show.\n95:$ SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_FORCE_LOCAL=1 python3 .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill_advisor.py 'create a readme for the utils folder' | jq -c '[.[0:3][] | {skill, kind, source, passes_threshold}]'\n96:Native advisor unavailable (FORCE_LOCAL; freshness=unavailable); falling back to local Python scorer.\n109:{\"status\":\"fresh\",\"counts\":{\"commandMetadata\":23,\"allowList\":4,\"doctorRoutes\":35,\"generated\":62,\"typescriptActive\":45,\"pythonActive\":51}}\n112:$ jq -c '[.python[].id | select(test(\"spec-kit\"))]' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json\n186:- A stated contract for a degraded result. The local Python scorer returns `command-create-readme` as a passing row for a plain prompt.\n187:- The four allow-list ids, the Python `\"/prompt\"` lexical row and owner branch, the two Python hand-authored constants and the optional `routingEnabled` type.\n201:- Retire the allow-list file, its four ids and the Python `/prompt` residue, delete the Python hand-authored constants and make `routingEnabled` required (L7).\n213:- The Python-only ids `command-spec-kit-deep-research` and `command-spec-kit-deep-review`, the TypeScript compatibility ids `create:agent` and `create:manual-testing-playbook`, and the alias folds that map old ids onto live ones. The operator chose to rename only the four allow-list ids.\n214:- Typed `/memory:save` as prompt vocabulary in `explicit.ts`, `fusion.ts`, the Python scorer and the Gate 3 classifier. It matches what a user types, and five labelled corpus rows type it.\n231:| `ADV/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json` | Modify | Four Python rows and one owner key deleted |\n266:| REQ-010 | The Python `\"/prompt\"` lexical row and the `command == \"/prompt\"` owner branch are deleted. The alias folds in `aliases.ts` and the Python alias table stay. |\n267:| REQ-011 | `HAND_AUTHORED_COMMAND_BRIDGES` and `HAND_AUTHORED_COMMAND_BRIDGE_OWNER_NORMALIZATION` are deleted from the Python scorer. `CommandBridgeProjection.routingEnabled` is required and `scoringCommandBridges` keeps rows with `routingEnabled === true`. |\n346:| Scope | 14/25 | About 24 files and 700 lines across the deriver, the handler, the renderer, the CLI, the Python scorer and tests |\n361:- How far does the id retirement go? Decision: \"Rename the four, drop /prompt (Recommended)\". The four allow-list ids become `command-speckit-*`, the Python `/prompt` residue goes, the alias folds stay, and the Python deep ids and the TypeScript `create:*` compatibility ids stay as a recorded limitation. REQ-018 does not need their rename, because `COMMAND_ROWS` keys `create:agent` and `create:manual-testing-playbook` as they are, so both carry `ownerSkillId` `sk-doc`.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"rg -n \\\"Python|python\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/spec.md | head -30\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794528250626,"end":1794528251849}}}}
