{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794528447469,"sessionID":"ses_e2dcb0a25ffeKDrFVYdzDGhvxv","part":{"partID":"prt_1d23b0850001Ec0ECf0b5tac9t","sessionID":"ses_e2dcb0a25ffeKDrFVYdzDGhvxv","messageID":"msg_1d23afe030016pbVs7d8eyQsNO","type":"tool","id":"call_28c78dba95274e35ad36496b","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n \"Python|PY\\b|skill_advisor|four ids|re-point\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/plan.md | head -60","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"23:| **Language/Stack** | TypeScript on Node, one CommonJS deriver, the Python fallback scorer |\n26:| **Testing** | Vitest through `npm test` in `ADV`, the Python test script, the routing-accuracy captures and the sk-doc reach check |\n58:- **Command table** (`ADV/lib/command-attach.ts`, generated by `derive-command-bridges.cjs`): `COMMAND_ROWS` maps every id a scorer can return for a command entry, the TypeScript id, the Python id and the inventory id, to `{ command, policy, ownerSkillId }`. `COMMAND_POLICIES` maps each runnable string to its policy. Without it each reader would rebuild the join from `commandPolicies`, the doctor details and the projection.\n60:- **Brief head** (`ADV/lib/render.ts`): a recommendation with a command renders `use <owner> → <command> (<policy>)`, where the owner is `ownerSkillId` or, for a hub with an attached command, the hub id. Fields win, and `COMMAND_ROWS` fills a missing field by id, which covers an older daemon and the Python subprocess path.\n118:| Integration | The pinned capture, the default command capture, the derive check, the rollup and the Python test script | The capture scripts, `jq`, `python3` |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"23:| **Language/Stack** | TypeScript on Node, one CommonJS deriver, the Python fallback scorer |\n26:| **Testing** | Vitest through `npm test` in `ADV`, the Python test script, the routing-accuracy captures and the sk-doc reach check |\n58:- **Command table** (`ADV/lib/command-attach.ts`, generated by `derive-command-bridges.cjs`): `COMMAND_ROWS` maps every id a scorer can return for a command entry, the TypeScript id, the Python id and the inventory id, to `{ command, policy, ownerSkillId }`. `COMMAND_POLICIES` maps each runnable string to its policy. Without it each reader would rebuild the join from `commandPolicies`, the doctor details and the projection.\n60:- **Brief head** (`ADV/lib/render.ts`): a recommendation with a command renders `use <owner> → <command> (<policy>)`, where the owner is `ownerSkillId` or, for a hub with an attached command, the hub id. Fields win, and `COMMAND_ROWS` fills a missing field by id, which covers an older daemon and the Python subprocess path.\n118:| Integration | The pinned capture, the default command capture, the derive check, the rollup and the Python test script | The capture scripts, `jq`, `python3` |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"rg -n \\\"Python|PY\\\\b|skill_advisor|four ids|re-point\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/plan.md | head -60\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794528446544,"end":1794528447469}}}}
